{"mls":"R1720849","addr":"15 McKenzie Street","muni":"Bergen village","town":"Bergen","county":"Genesee","zip":"14416","ll":[43.082103,-77.94173],"status":"Active","type":"Single Family","units":1,"beds":4,"baths":2,"sqft":2297.0,"year":1874,"lot":0.35,"dom":4,"price":239900,"orig":null,"chg":"New Listing","tax":8503,"tax_mls":true,"hoa":null,"office":"Howard Hanna","phone":"petergonzales@howardhanna.com","hhp":false,"remarks":"Welcome to 15 McKenzie Street, where timeless colonial charm meets modern updates in the heart of the Village of Bergen! This spacious 4-bedroom, 2-full-bath home sits on a 0.35-acre lot and immediately impresses with its distinctive gambrel-style roofline, charming dormer windows, crisp white siding, inviting enclosed front porch, and beautifully landscaped entryway. Inside, discover an expansive dining room featuring a wood stove, recently cleaned and ready for winter! The updated kitchen boasts granite countertops, stainless steel appliances, abundant cabinetry, and generous storage. Laminate flooring flows throughout the main first-floor living areas. Enjoy the convenience of a first-floor primary bedroom with an attached full bathroom and first-floor laundry! A spacious rear living room, additional full bathroom, and dedicated home office with vinyl flooring offer flexibility for everyday living. Upstairs features three additional bedrooms, including one with NEW carpeting (April 2026), while the remaining two feature vinyl flooring. Both full bathrooms have been updated within the last 10 years! Major improvements include a updated METAL ROOF WITH TRANSFERABLE WARRANTY, updated furnace and hot water tank, 200-amp electrical service, vinyl windows throughout, and vinyl siding. A full basement provides additional storage. Step outside to your private backyard retreat, fully enclosed with vinyl and wood fencing! Enjoy entertaining on the rear deck featuring composite boards and vinyl railings. Additional highlights include a 1.5-car detached garage with wood siding and an additional in-house garage space perfect for lawn equipment or seasonal storage. Enjoy village living with convenient access to Greg'ry's Bakery, Ralph & Rosie's Deli, Hickory Park's playground and recreational facilities, Hartland Park's disc golf course, the Byron-Bergen Public Library and nearby Gillam-Grant Community Center offers recreational programs. Explore the historic village streets or enjoy convenient access to Rochester and Batavia! Delayed negotiations until Tuesday, October 20th at 12:00 PM.","facts":[["Total rooms","10"],["Full baths","2"],["Half baths","0"],["Style","Colonial, Historic Antique"],["Levels","Two"],["Stories","2"],["Building area (sq ft)","2,297"],["Heating","Gas, Forced Air"],["Basement","Full"],["Foundation","Block, Stone"],["Construction","Vinyl Siding, Copper Plumbing"],["Roof","Architectural, Metal, Shingle"],["Garage","Yes"],["Garage spaces","1.5"],["Parking","Detached, Electricity, Garage, Garage Door Opener, Shared Driveway"],["Utilities","Cable Available, Electricity Connected, High Speed Internet Available, Sewer Connected, Water Connected"],["Electric","Circuit Breakers"],["Sewer","Connected"],["Water","Connected, Public"],["Appliances","Dryer, Dishwasher, Exhaust Fan, Disposal, Gas Oven, Gas Range, Gas Water Heater, Microwave, Refrigerator, Range Hood, Washer"],["Flooring","Carpet, Laminate, Resilient, Tile, Varies, Vinyl"],["Interior features","Breakfast Bar, Ceiling Fans, Separate Formal Dining Room, Separate Formal Living Room, Granite Counters, Home Office, Sliding Glass Doors, Natural Woodwork, Bedroom On Main Level, Bath In Primary Bedroom, Main Level Primary"],["Exterior features","Blacktop Driveway, Deck, Enclosed Porch, Fully Fenced, Hot Tub Spa, Porch"],["Waterfront","No"],["Lot dimensions","63 X231"],["Lot features","Rectangular, Rectangular Lot, Residential Lot"],["Elementary school district","Byron-Bergen"],["High school district","Byron-Bergen"],["Assessed value","$258,000"]],